# Credentials configuration template
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual credentials.
#
# ⚠️ bootstrap/.env is gitignored — it does NOT travel with the repo. When you
#    run the bridge from a NEW checkout or machine, you MUST recreate it here.
#    bridge/run.sh sources bootstrap/.env at start; if it's missing, every GitHub
#    push/PR silently fails (github-identity.sh: "JARVIS_GITHUB_TOKEN is required")
#    and release-flow tickets stall at jarvis-idle with no obvious error.
#    Self-check after setup:  bootstrap/github-identity.sh check   (must print api-tool-agent)
#    Note: exporting the token only in ~/.zshrc is NOT enough — the bridge starts
#    via launchd/nohup (non-interactive shell) and won't inherit .zshrc exports.

# GitHub push / PR token. This is the var the code actually reads
# (github-identity.sh, claim.sh) — NOT a bare GH_TOKEN. Account MUST be api-tool-agent.
JARVIS_GITHUB_TOKEN=
ALIYUN_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
ALIYUN_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET=
JARVIS_HTML_REPORT_TOKEN=
# a1: 容器内凭证, 无需手填
